# Tests for the spike toy

> Using Spike_rate

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope T1:
  s1 scope Spike_rate.TaxSchedule
  s2 scope Spike_rate.TaxSchedule
  s3 scope Spike_rate.TaxSchedule
  s4 scope Spike_rate.TaxSchedule

scope T1:
  definition s1.filing_status equals Spike_rate.FilingStatus.Single
  definition s1.taxable_income equals $50,000
  definition s2.filing_status equals Spike_rate.FilingStatus.Single
  definition s2.taxable_income equals $1,000,000
  definition s3.filing_status equals Spike_rate.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
  definition s3.taxable_income equals $3
  definition s4.filing_status equals Spike_rate.FilingStatus.HeadOfHousehold
  definition s4.taxable_income equals $2,999
  # IRS 2024 Tax Table: Single 50,000-50,050 is 6,059
  assertion (s1.tax = $6,059)
  assertion (s2.tax = $328,188)
  assertion (s3.tax = $0)
  assertion (s4.tax = $299)
```
